    "text_blocks": [
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "snippet": "Metal roofing lasts longer and handles Utah's heavy snow and intense UV rays better than asphalt shingles, but asphalt shingles cost significantly less upfront.",
        "snippet_highlighted_words": [
          "Metal roofing lasts longer and handles Utah's heavy snow and intense UV rays better than asphalt shingles"
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "snippet": "Cost Comparison"
      },
      {
        "type": "list",
        "list": [
          {
            "snippet": "Asphalt Shingles: Costs between $10,000 and $18,000 installed."
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Metal Roofing: Costs between $15,000 and $35,000 installed, roughly double the price of asphalt."
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Value: Asphalt is better if you plan to sell your home soon. Metal is a better long-term investment if you plan to stay for decades."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "snippet": "Lifespan and Weather in Utah"
      },
      {
        "type": "list",
        "list": [
          {
            "snippet": "Asphalt Shingles: Lasts 15 to 30 years. Utah's extreme summer heat, high-altitude UV rays, and winter freeze-thaw cycles can crack and shorten their lifespan."
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Metal Roofing: Lasts 40 to 70 years or more. It resists warping, shrinking, and UV damage."
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Snow and Ice: Metal has a slick surface that helps heavy snow slide right off, which prevents dangerous ice dams and lowers structural stress. Asphalt traps more snow and ice on its textured surface."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "snippet": "Learn more about how metal roofs compare to asphalt shingles in durability, cost, and quality:"
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "snippet": "Maintenance and Repairs"
      },
      {
        "type": "list",
        "list": [
          {
            "snippet": "Asphalt Shingles: Easier and cheaper to repair or patch when damaged. They are heavier and put more weight on a home's structure over multiple layers."
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Metal Roofing: Harder to repair or install, but acts as a long-lasting \"one and done\" system that needs very little upkeep. Thicker gauges (like 24-gauge over 26-gauge) resist hail dents and oil-canning waviness."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "snippet": "If you'd like, tell me:"
      },
      {
        "type": "list",
        "list": [
          {
            "snippet": "Are you planning to stay in the home long-term or sell soon?"
          },
          {
            "snippet": "What city or mountain area in Utah is the home located in?"
          }
        ]
      },
